# Copy to `.env` and edit. `.env` is gitignored -- never commit real tokens.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# Two groups below, and the difference is load-bearing:
#
#   GROUP 1 is read by Docker Compose itself, to fill the `${VAR}` slots in
#   docker-compose.yml. These are the ones that actually change a
#   `docker compose up`.
#
#   GROUP 2 is read by the application. Under Compose these are already set
#   in each service's `environment:` block, so setting them here changes
#   nothing -- they matter when you run the API or CLI directly on your host
#   (`uv run uvicorn server.app:app`).
#
# Everything here is optional. With an empty .env, `docker compose up` and the
# whole CLI still work; the optional generation features just report
# themselves as unavailable instead. Run `cinemagraph doctor` to see what's
# configured and what isn't.


# ============================================================================
# GROUP 1 -- read by Docker Compose (${VAR} substitution)
# ============================================================================

# Hugging Face token, required by the `sound-effects` service and nothing else.
#
# stabilityai/stable-audio-open-1.0 is a GATED repository: you must visit the
# model page and accept its license with the same account this token belongs
# to, or the download fails no matter how valid the token is. That is the most
# common first-run failure with this project, and it is not a bug here.
#
#   1. https://huggingface.co/stabilityai/stable-audio-open-1.0  -> accept
#   2. https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens  -> create a read token
#
# HF_TOKEN=hf_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Google AI Studio key. Optional, and unrelated to the self-hosted services:
# it enables the hosted `gemini` image backend and `lyria3` music backend,
# which need no container and no GPU. Absent -> those two adapters simply
# never register, and `GET /capabilities` won't list them.
#
#   https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#
# Note the account caveat recorded in docs/experiments/: new Google AI Studio
# accounts have required a non-refundable minimum prepay before the image API
# is usable at all.
#
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# --- Model lifecycle, applied to all three satellites ----------------------
# Full explanation in each satellite's README ("Model lifecycle") and in
# docs/experiments/2026-08-21-model-lifecycle-prior-art.md.

# Seconds a model may sit idle before it's unloaded and its VRAM released.
# 0 = keep it resident forever (Immich's semantics, which this follows).
# This exists because the satellites are effectively mutually exclusive on an
# 8GB card -- SDXL alone takes ~7.1GB -- so with a TTL they take turns.
# MODEL_TTL=900

# Seconds a single request may run before the service concludes it is wedged
# and exits, so the container restarts and the driver gets the GPU back.
# 0 disables it. Keep this comfortably above your slowest legitimate request:
# a cold load plus a generation, which has been measured as high as ~6 minutes
# for SDXL. Killing a slow-but-healthy job is worse than waiting out a stuck one.
# BUSY_TIMEOUT=1200


# ============================================================================
# GROUP 2 -- read by the app; only needed when running outside Compose
# ============================================================================

# --- Where things are written ---------------------------------------------

# Per-job scratch space for the API (uploads, renders). Compose sets this to
# /data, which is host-mounted.
# CINEMAGRAPH_DATA_DIR=./data

# The asset library: content-addressed storage plus its SQLite index. Kept
# deliberately independent of CINEMAGRAPH_DATA_DIR, because the library must
# work from the CLI alone with no server running. Defaults to
# ~/.cinemagraph/library -- which inside a container is a throwaway path, which
# is why Compose overrides it to /data/library.
# CINEMAGRAPH_LIBRARY_DIR=

# The built web UI that GET / serves. Defaults to this repo's frontend/dist,
# so a source checkout needs `bun run build` once and nothing here. If the
# directory is missing, the UI routes explain how to build it and every other
# route keeps working.
# CINEMAGRAPH_FRONTEND_DIR=

# --- Optional service URLs -------------------------------------------------
# Each is read at REQUEST time, never at startup. Unset or unreachable means
# that one feature reports itself unavailable (503 from its route, false from
# GET /capabilities); the app always starts and everything else keeps working.
# Under Compose these already point at the right service names.

# ML_SERVICE_URL=http://localhost:8004        # machine-learning (CLIPSeg masks)
# ACESTEP_URL=http://localhost:8001           # ACE-Step (music)
# SOUND_EFFECTS_URL=http://localhost:8003     # Stable Audio Open (sound effects)
# IMAGE_GENERATION_URL=http://localhost:8005  # SDXL (images)

# --- Per-satellite knobs ---------------------------------------------------

# Load the model at startup instead of on the first request. Off by default:
# eager loading is exactly what made these services hold the GPU while idle.
# PRELOAD=0

# image-generation only. Keeps SDXL's weights in host RAM and moves each
# sub-model onto the GPU only while it runs: measured at 147 MiB resident VRAM
# instead of 7147 MiB, for ~2.5GB more host RAM and no reliable speed cost.
# On by default. Set to 0 if this service shares a host with something else
# memory-hungry. See docs/experiments/2026-08-18-sdxl-cpu-offload.md.
# CPU_OFFLOAD=1

# Where each satellite caches downloaded weights. Set in the Dockerfiles and
# backed by a named volume in Compose -- override only if running a satellite
# directly on the host.
# HF_HOME=


# ============================================================================
# Development only
# ============================================================================

# Backend the frontend dev server proxies API calls to (`bun run dev`).
# VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:8000

# Base URL for the live integration tests, which are deselected by default.
# CINEMAGRAPH_TEST_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
